1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:04,460
That clear water dripping from your air conditioner? Don't drink it.

2
00:00:05,350 --> 00:00:07,000
It is condensation.

3
00:00:07,030 --> 00:00:14,060
Warm, humid room air touches the cold coil, the moisture turns into drops, and they run into a pan and out the pipe.

4
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:18,520
The same coil also pulls moisture out of your air, so the room gets dry,

5
00:00:18,550 --> 00:00:22,080
and dry air can irritate your skin, eyes and throat.

6
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:29,260
In a closed bedroom, many room air conditioners just recirculate the air, so carbon dioxide builds up overnight.

7
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:31,720
Studies link that to less deep sleep.

8
00:00:31,870 --> 00:00:33,720
Let some fresh air in.

9
00:00:34,350 --> 00:00:38,920
Now the catch. On its way out, the water touches the coil, the pan and the pipe.

10
00:00:39,250 --> 00:00:45,060
Germs can build up there, including, in some systems, the bacteria behind Legionnaires disease.

11
00:00:45,410 --> 00:00:49,160
Parts can also add metals like copper, and lead from solder.

12
00:00:50,350 --> 00:00:53,520
So drain it, or water your plants. Don't drink it.

13
00:01:00,850 --> 00:01:03,620
Like, share and subscribe for more explainers.
